and autonomous marketing assistant designed to automate and accelerate marketing strategy, content creation, and campaign execution; Customer Agent, an AI-powered assistant that provides support and selling across digital channels; Klaviyo Social, which brings social interaction data into the company's unified consumer profiles; and Marketing Analytics that provide real-time AI-powered insights into consumer purchase. In addition, the company offers email marketing solutions comprising a range of customizable drag-and-drop templates, automated campaign and workflow capabilities, smart send time optimization, generative AI tools, and A/B testing; mobile messaging capabilities through text messaging, rich communication services, and WhatsApp; personalized push notifications; reviews add-on to collect product reviews, consumer data, and messaging; and integration, segmentation, automation, and analytics and benchmark features for its platform. Further, it provides Customer Hub, a consumer-facing portal that brings shopping, service, and personalization together in one place; and Helpdesk, an AI-powered workspace for managing consumer conversations across channels. The company serves entrepreneurs, small and medium-sized businesses, mid-market businesses, and enterprises. Klaviyo, Inc. was incorporated in 2012 and is headquartered in Boston, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Andrew  Bialecki | Co-Founder, Co-CEO & Chairperson | Age 38 | Compensation: $78,000 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $513K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 33%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $87K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $67K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Klaviyo, Inc. Series A is a mid-cap technology business with a $6.2B market cap on $1.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +33% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +20.9pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -51% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 75% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $209M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 17 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 13% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 108% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.0757043973179141},{"text":"Operating margins 12% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $96.0M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 9919% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Technology peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Reviewing Docebo (NASDAQ:DCBO) & Klaviyo (NYSE:KVYO)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/reviewing-docebo-nasdaqdcbo-klaviyo-nysekvyo.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794590183.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.945,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How Investors Are Reacting To Klaviyo (KVYO) Earnings Estimate Upgrades","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/software/nyse-kvyo/klaviyo/news/how-investors-are-reacting-to-klaviyo-kvyo-earnings-estimate","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794554218.066,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.66,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","analyst_action"]},{"title":"Earnings Estimates Rising for Klaviyo, Inc. (KVYO): Will It Gain?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028929/earnings-estimates-rising-for-klaviyo-inc-kvyo-will-it-gain?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_8-3028929","date":"2026-11-12","timesta